{
  "model": "IndexTeam/IndexTTS-2.5",
  "voice": "温暖自然英式女老师｜IndexTTS2.5 慢速教学",
  "pause_seconds": 0.7,
  "chunks": [
    {
      "id": "s43-p01",
      "text": "After it rains, we put away our umbrellas.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s43-p02",
      "text": "Then we may see rainbows in the sky above us.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s43-p03",
      "text": "The conditions need to be just right to see a rainbow.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p03.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p03.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s43-p04",
      "text": "We need some water drops in the air, like rain, fog or clouds.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p04.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p04.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s43-p05",
      "text": "And we need the sun to be behind us and low to the ground, which often happens in the autumn.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p05.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p05.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s43-p06",
      "text": "Because a rainbow is created by light passing through water drops.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p06.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p06.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s43-p07",
      "text": "As the name suggests, rainbows are supposed to be the shape of a bow.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p07.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p07.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s43-p08",
      "text": "Neither the sun nor the water drops are the same every time, so each rainbow is unique.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p08.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p08.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s43-p09",
      "text": "Rainbows could also look like some colourful smoke.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p09.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p09.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s43-p10-01",
      "text": "The light that comes from the sun seems white to us,",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p10-01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p10-01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s43-p10-02",
      "text": "but the white light is actually a mix of different colours.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p10-02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p10-02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s43-p11",
      "text": "When the light goes through a raindrop, these colours can separate out.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p11.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p11.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s43-p12",
      "text": "Raindrops look like little balls.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p12.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p12.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s43-p13",
      "text": "When light hits one of these little balls, it changes direction.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p13.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p13.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s43-p14",
      "text": "We call this refraction.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p14.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p14.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s43-p15",
      "text": "Lights of different wavelengths are refracted differently, so they are separated out into different colours.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p15.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p15.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s43-p16",
      "text": "In a rainbow, there are seven colours arranged in a row: red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo and violet.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p16.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p16.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s43-p17",
      "text": "While colours like brown and pink are not usually seen.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p17.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p17.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s43-p18",
      "text": "And we would never see black and white in a rainbow.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p18.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p18.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s43-p19",
      "text": "Black is what we see when there's no light, while white is a mix of all the colours together.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p19.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p19.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s43-p20",
      "text": "The science of rainbows is fascinating.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p20.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p20.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s43-p21",
      "text": "Even on a busy weekday, we should look up to the sky.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p21.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p21.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s43-p22",
      "text": "It's an easy way to appreciate the beauty of nature.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p22.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s43-p22.mp3"
    }
  ],
  "word_audio": "browser speech synthesis en-GB"
}
